+"""
+Secure aggregation production wrapper (integration scaffold).
+
+This module provides a stable interface the FL server/client should use.
+It tries to use a vetted secure-aggregation implementation if available on the system
+-- otherwise it falls back to the additive-mask approach while refusing to run in
+production (requires explicit opt-in).
+
+Recommended production integration:
+- Use a vetted implementation (e.g., Google's secagg reference, an audited library,
+  or an implementation maintained by your chosen FL framework).
+- Run an external crypto review of the chosen implementation.
+
+API:
+ - server_prepare_round(round_id, participants) -> server metadata
+ - client_prepare_keys(client_id) -> (private_key_bytes, public_key_b64)
+ - client_mask_and_upload(client_id, round_id, weights) -> masked_update
+ - server_finalize_round(round_id) -> aggregated_result
+
+This file does NOT implement full Bonawitz secure aggregation; it is an integration shim.
+"""
